IMPORT prelude

-- Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (Qld) -- the seat-neutral core.
--
-- Written from the deposited text (act-1987-088, the version in force from 2011-01-01, current on 6 November 2026),
-- in the Act's own actors and terms: the Supreme Court (of Queensland), the Supreme Court of another State or of a
-- Territory, the State Family Court, the Federal Court, the Family Court, the first court, the party. Each rule is
-- preceded by the words it encodes. Judgments the Act leaves to a court ("it appears to the Supreme Court", "in the
-- opinion of", "the interests of justice", "special reasons", "a reasonable time") are inputs, never decided here.
-- Borrowed terms (special federal matter, the Schedule to the Commonwealth Act, the ADJR enactment paragraphs, the
-- Australian Consumer Law provisions) are asked as facts.
--
-- Answers follow the corpus conventions: JUST FALSE where the text itself says no ("means", "if", "where", "shall
-- not", "does not"), NOTHING where it is silent or "includes" without closing the list. The fork lines are in NOTES.md.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (Qld) -- core`

§§ `Dates`

GIVEN `n`         IS A NUMBER
      `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `n` `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL ((DATE_SERIAL `the start`) PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `a` `to` `b` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `b` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `a`

§§ `The courts and the parties`

-- The courts the Act names. "State includes the Northern Territory and the Australian Capital Territory";
-- "Territory does not include the Northern Territory or the Australian Capital Territory" (s 3(1)), so the Supreme
-- Courts of the NT and the ACT are Supreme Courts "of another State".
DECLARE `Court` IS ONE OF
    `the Supreme Court of Queensland`
    `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory`
    `the State Family Court of another State`
    `the Federal Court`
    `the Family Court`
    `a court of Queensland other than the Supreme Court`
    `a tribunal established by or under an Act`
    `some other court`

-- "party, in relation to a proceeding, includes a person who intervenes in the proceeding" (s 3(1)).
DECLARE `Role in the proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `a party`
    `a person who intervenes`
    `someone else`

GIVEN `my role` IS A `Role in the proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a party (s 3(1))` `my role` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `a party` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person who intervenes` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 3, s 3A -- what the Act applies to`

-- s 3(1) "proceeding does not include a criminal proceeding."
-- s 3A "This Act does not apply to the jurisdiction of courts with which the Corporations Act, part 9.6A, division 1
-- deals."
GIVEN `it is a criminal proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is within Corporations Act part 9.6A division 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Act can apply to the proceeding (ss 3, 3A)` `it is a criminal proceeding` `it is within Corporations Act part 9.6A division 1` MEANS
    IF `it is a criminal proceeding` OR `it is within Corporations Act part 9.6A division 1`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 3(1) "State matter means a matter-- (a) in which the Supreme Court has jurisdiction otherwise than by reason of a
-- law of the Commonwealth or of another State; or (b) removed to the Supreme Court under section 8."
GIVEN `the Supreme Court has jurisdiction otherwise than by a Commonwealth or other State law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter was removed to the Supreme Court under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a State matter (s 3(1))` `the Supreme Court has jurisdiction otherwise than by a Commonwealth or other State law` `the matter was removed to the Supreme Court under section 8` IF
        `the Supreme Court has jurisdiction otherwise than by a Commonwealth or other State law`
    OR  `the matter was removed to the Supreme Court under section 8`

§§ `s 4 -- vesting of additional jurisdiction`

-- s 4(1) "The Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory has and may exercise original and appellate
-- jurisdiction with respect to State matters."
-- s 4(2) "The State Family Court of another State has and may exercise original and appellate jurisdiction with
-- respect to State matters."
-- s 4(3) "Subsection (1) or (2) does not-- (a) invest ... or (b) confer ... jurisdiction with respect to criminal
-- matters."
GIVEN `the court` IS A `Court`
      `it is a State matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the court has jurisdiction in the State matter under s 4` `the court` `it is a State matter` `it is a criminal matter` MEANS
    IF `it is a criminal matter`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it is a State matter` AND `the court is one s 4 names`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the court is one s 4 names` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the court`
            WHEN `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the State Family Court of another State` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 5 -- transfer of proceedings`

DECLARE `Transfer answer` IS ONE OF
    `the first court must transfer it`
    `the first court may transfer it, but need not`
    `this provision does not require a transfer on these facts`
    `the Act does not deal with a transfer between these courts`

-- The facts a court's s 5 transfer turns on. Each "it appears to the first court" opinion is an input.
DECLARE `Transfer facts` HAS
    `the first court` IS A `Court`
    `the other court` IS A `Court`
    `a related proceeding is pending in the other court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the first court finds the other court more appropriate because of the related proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the first court finds the other court more appropriate having regard to the s 5 factors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the first court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `section 6A applies to the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 5(1) "If-- (a) a proceeding ... is pending in the Supreme Court; and (b) it appears to the Supreme Court that,
-- having regard to-- (i) ... (ii) ... (iii) the interests of justice; it is more appropriate that the relevant
-- proceeding be determined by the Federal Court or the Family Court ...; the Supreme Court must transfer the
-- relevant proceeding ..."
-- s 6A(3) "If-- (a) the federal matter proceeding is pending in the Supreme Court; and (b) the State matter proceeding
-- is pending in any court of this State; neither section 5(1) nor section 6 applies to require the Supreme Court to
-- transfer ... but the Supreme Court may do so if it considers that to be appropriate ..."
GIVEN `f` IS A `Transfer facts`
GIVETH A `Transfer answer`
`s 5(1) -- Supreme Court to the Federal Court or the Family Court` `f` MEANS
    IF `f`'s `section 6A applies to the proceeding`
    THEN `the first court may transfer it, but need not`
    ELSE IF `f`'s `the first court finds the other court more appropriate having regard to the s 5 factors`
         THEN `the first court must transfer it`
         ELSE `this provision does not require a transfer on these facts`

-- s 5(2) "Where-- (a) a proceeding ... is pending in the Supreme Court (the first court); and (b) it appears to the
-- first court that-- (i) the relevant proceeding arises out of, or is related to, another proceeding pending in the
-- Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory and it is more appropriate that the relevant proceeding be
-- determined by that other Supreme Court; or (ii) having regard to-- (A) ... (B) ... (C) the interests of justice; it
-- is more appropriate that the relevant proceeding be determined by that other Supreme Court; or (iii) it is
-- otherwise in the interests of justice that the relevant proceeding be determined by the Supreme Court of another
-- State or of a Territory; the first court shall transfer the relevant proceeding to that other Supreme Court."
-- s 5(3) is the mirror, from the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory to the Supreme Court of Queensland.
GIVEN `f` IS A `Transfer facts`
GIVETH A `Transfer answer`
`s 5(2), (3) -- between Supreme Courts` `f` MEANS
    IF     (    `f`'s `a related proceeding is pending in the other court`
            AND `f`'s `the first court finds the other court more appropriate because of the related proceeding`)
        OR `f`'s `the first court finds the other court more appropriate having regard to the s 5 factors`
        OR `f`'s `the first court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice`
    THEN `the first court must transfer it`
    ELSE `this provision does not require a transfer on these facts`

-- s 5(4) "Where-- (a) a proceeding ... is pending in the Federal Court or the Family Court (the first court); and (b)
-- it appears to the first court that-- (i) the relevant proceeding arises out of, or is related to, another
-- proceeding pending in the Supreme Court and it is more appropriate that the relevant proceeding be determined by
-- the Supreme Court; or (ii) having regard to-- (A) ... (B) ... (C) ... (D) the interests of justice; it is more
-- appropriate that the relevant proceeding be determined by the Supreme Court; or (iii) it is otherwise in the
-- interests of justice that the relevant proceeding be determined by the Supreme Court; the first court shall
-- transfer the relevant proceeding to the Supreme Court."
-- s 6A(2) "... the Federal Court or the Family Court may transfer the proceeding to the Supreme Court, and section
-- 5(4) does not apply to the proceeding."
GIVEN `f` IS A `Transfer facts`
GIVETH A `Transfer answer`
`s 5(4) -- Federal Court or Family Court to the Supreme Court` `f` MEANS
    IF `f`'s `section 6A applies to the proceeding`
    THEN `the first court may transfer it, but need not`
    ELSE `s 5(2), (3) -- between Supreme Courts` `f`

-- Which of s 5(1)-(4) the two courts call up. A pair s 5 does not name is "not dealt with" by this Act (the
-- Commonwealth Act and the other States' Acts deal with their own courts).
GIVEN `f` IS A `Transfer facts`
GIVETH A `Transfer answer`
`the s 5 transfer answer` `f` MEANS
    CONSIDER `f`'s `the first court`
    WHEN `the Supreme Court of Queensland` THEN
        CONSIDER `f`'s `the other court`
        WHEN `the Federal Court` THEN `s 5(1) -- Supreme Court to the Federal Court or the Family Court` `f`
        WHEN `the Family Court` THEN `s 5(1) -- Supreme Court to the Federal Court or the Family Court` `f`
        WHEN `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` THEN `s 5(2), (3) -- between Supreme Courts` `f`
        OTHERWISE `the Act does not deal with a transfer between these courts`
    WHEN `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` THEN
        CONSIDER `f`'s `the other court`
        WHEN `the Supreme Court of Queensland` THEN `s 5(2), (3) -- between Supreme Courts` `f`
        OTHERWISE `the Act does not deal with a transfer between these courts`
    WHEN `the Federal Court` THEN
        CONSIDER `f`'s `the other court`
        WHEN `the Supreme Court of Queensland` THEN `s 5(4) -- Federal Court or Family Court to the Supreme Court` `f`
        OTHERWISE `the Act does not deal with a transfer between these courts`
    WHEN `the Family Court` THEN
        CONSIDER `f`'s `the other court`
        WHEN `the Supreme Court of Queensland` THEN `s 5(4) -- Federal Court or Family Court to the Supreme Court` `f`
        OTHERWISE `the Act does not deal with a transfer between these courts`
    OTHERWISE `the Act does not deal with a transfer between these courts`

-- s 5(6) "Where-- (a) a court (the first court) transfers a proceeding to another court under a law or laws relating
-- to cross-vesting of jurisdiction; and (b) it appears to the first court that-- (i) there is another proceeding
-- pending in the first court that arises out of, or is related to, the first mentioned proceeding; and (ii) it is in
-- the interests of justice that the other proceeding be determined by the other court; the first court shall
-- transfer the other proceeding to the other court."
GIVEN `the first court transferred a proceeding under a cross-vesting law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another related proceeding is pending in the first court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first court finds it in the interests of justice that the other court determine it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the related proceeding must follow (s 5(6))` `the first court transferred a proceeding under a cross-vesting law` `another related proceeding is pending in the first court` `the first court finds it in the interests of justice that the other court determine it` IF
        `the first court transferred a proceeding under a cross-vesting law`
    AND `another related proceeding is pending in the first court`
    AND `the first court finds it in the interests of justice that the other court determine it`

-- s 5(7) "A court may transfer a proceeding under this section on the application of a party to the proceeding, of
-- its own motion or on the application of the Attorney-General ..." The list is not closed with "only".
GIVEN `my role` IS A `Role in the proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`may apply for a transfer (s 5(7))` `my role` MEANS `is a party (s 3(1))` `my role`

-- s 5(8) "A person who is entitled to practise as a barrister or a solicitor ... in a court has, if a proceeding (the
-- transferred proceeding) in that court is transferred to another court under a law or laws relating to
-- cross-vesting of jurisdiction, the same entitlement to practise in relation to-- (a) the transferred proceedings; and
-- (b) any other proceeding out of which the transferred proceeding arises or to which the transferred proceeding is
-- related, being another proceeding that is to be determined together with the transferred proceeding; in the other
-- court that the person would have if the other court were a federal court exercising federal jurisdiction."
GIVEN `the lawyer may practise in the first court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding was transferred under a cross-vesting law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the transferred proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a related proceeding to be determined together with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the lawyer may practise in the other court (s 5(8))` `the lawyer may practise in the first court` `the proceeding was transferred under a cross-vesting law` `it is the transferred proceeding` `it is a related proceeding to be determined together with it` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceeding was transferred under a cross-vesting law`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF     `the lawyer may practise in the first court`
            AND (`it is the transferred proceeding` OR `it is a related proceeding to be determined together with it`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 6 -- special federal matters`

-- "special federal matter has the same meaning as in the Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (Cwlth)"
-- (s 3(1)): borrowed, so its paragraph is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Special federal matter` IS ONE OF
    `none`
    `paragraph (a), (b) or (d) of the Commonwealth definition`
    `paragraph (c) or (e) of the Commonwealth definition`
    `paragraph (ab) of the Commonwealth definition`

DECLARE `Special federal matter answer` IS ONE OF
    `section 6 does not apply: there is no special federal matter`
    `section 6 deals only with a proceeding pending in the Supreme Court`
    `section 6 does not apply to this appeal (s 6(9))`
    `the Supreme Court may keep it: it has ordered under s 6(3) that it determine the proceeding`
    `section 6 does not require a transfer; the Supreme Court may still transfer it (s 6A(3))`
    `the part within the Federal Court's jurisdiction must go to the Federal Court`
    `the part within that court's jurisdiction must go to the Family Court, the Family Court of Western Australia or the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory, whichever the Supreme Court thinks appropriate`

-- s 6A(1) "This section applies to a proceeding (the federal matter proceeding) if-- (a) a matter for determination
-- in the proceeding is covered by paragraph (c) or (e) of the definition special federal matter ...; and (b) the
-- matter ... involves or relates to the exercise ... of functions or powers conferred on a Commonwealth authority, or
-- officer of the Commonwealth, by an enactment (the State enactment) referred to in paragraph (ca) or (cb) of the
-- definition enactment in section 3(1) of the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977 (Cwlth); and (c) the
-- matter ... arises out of, or relates to, another proceeding (the State matter proceeding) pending in any court of
-- this State-- (i) that arises, or a substantial part of which arises, under the State enactment or a corresponding
-- enactment of another State; and (ii) none of the matters for determination in which are covered by paragraph (c) or
-- (e) ...; regardless of which proceeding was commenced first."
GIVEN `the special federal matter` IS A `Special federal matter`
      `it concerns a Commonwealth authority or officer acting under a State enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a related State matter proceeding is pending in a Queensland court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that State matter proceeding arises substantially under the State enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that State matter proceeding has no paragraph (c) or (e) matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6A applies (s 6A(1))` `the special federal matter` `it concerns a Commonwealth authority or officer acting under a State enactment` `a related State matter proceeding is pending in a Queensland court` `that State matter proceeding arises substantially under the State enactment` `that State matter proceeding has no paragraph (c) or (e) matter` IF
        `it is paragraph (c) or (e)`
    AND `it concerns a Commonwealth authority or officer acting under a State enactment`
    AND `a related State matter proceeding is pending in a Queensland court`
    AND `that State matter proceeding arises substantially under the State enactment`
    AND `that State matter proceeding has no paragraph (c) or (e) matter`
    WHERE
        `it is paragraph (c) or (e)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the special federal matter`
            WHEN `paragraph (c) or (e) of the Commonwealth definition` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 6(1) "If-- (a) a matter for determination in a proceeding that is pending in the Supreme Court is a special
-- federal matter; and (b) the court does not make an order under subsection (3) in respect of the matter; the court
-- must transfer the proceeding in accordance with this section to the Federal Court or a court mentioned in
-- subsection (2)(b)."
-- s 6(1A) "However, the court must only transfer so much of the proceeding as is, in the opinion of the court, within
-- the jurisdiction (including the accrued jurisdiction) of the Federal Court, or the court mentioned in subsection
-- (2)(b), as the case may be."
-- s 6(2) "... (a) if the matter ... is a matter mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e) of the definition
-- ...--to the Federal Court; or (b) if the matter ... is a matter mentioned in paragraph (ab) of that definition--to
-- whichever of the Family Court, the Family Court of Western Australia or the Supreme Court of the Northern
-- Territory, in the opinion of the court, is appropriate in the circumstances."
-- s 6(9) "This section does not apply to a proceeding by way of an appeal that is instituted in the Full Court of the
-- Supreme Court if the court the decision of which is the subject of the appeal had made an order under subsection
-- (3) ... in relation to the special federal matter."
-- s 6A(3), above s 5(1).
GIVEN `pending in the Supreme Court of Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special federal matter` IS A `Special federal matter`
      `the Supreme Court has ordered under s 6(3) that it determine the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 6A applies to the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an appeal to the Full Court from a decision where the court below made an s 6(3) order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Special federal matter answer`
`the s 6 answer` `pending in the Supreme Court of Queensland` `the special federal matter` `the Supreme Court has ordered under s 6(3) that it determine the proceeding` `section 6A applies to the proceeding` `it is an appeal to the Full Court from a decision where the court below made an s 6(3) order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the special federal matter`
    WHEN `none` THEN `section 6 does not apply: there is no special federal matter`
    OTHERWISE
        IF NOT `pending in the Supreme Court of Queensland`
        THEN `section 6 deals only with a proceeding pending in the Supreme Court`
        ELSE IF `it is an appeal to the Full Court from a decision where the court below made an s 6(3) order`
             THEN `section 6 does not apply to this appeal (s 6(9))`
             ELSE IF `the Supreme Court has ordered under s 6(3) that it determine the proceeding`
                  THEN `the Supreme Court may keep it: it has ordered under s 6(3) that it determine the proceeding`
                  ELSE IF `section 6A applies to the proceeding`
                       THEN `section 6 does not require a transfer; the Supreme Court may still transfer it (s 6A(3))`
                       ELSE CONSIDER `the special federal matter`
                            WHEN `paragraph (ab) of the Commonwealth definition` THEN `the part within that court's jurisdiction must go to the Family Court, the Family Court of Western Australia or the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory, whichever the Supreme Court thinks appropriate`
                            OTHERWISE `the part within the Federal Court's jurisdiction must go to the Federal Court`

-- s 6(3) "The Supreme Court may order that the proceeding be determined by that court if it is satisfied that there
-- are special reasons for doing so in the particular circumstances of the proceeding other than reasons relevant to
-- the convenience of the parties."
-- s 6(4) "Before making an order under subsection (3), the court must be satisfied that-- (a) a written notice
-- specifying the nature of the special federal matter has been given to the Attorney-General of the Commonwealth and
-- the Attorney-General of the State; and (b) a reasonable time has elapsed since the giving of the notice for the
-- Attorneys-General to consider whether submissions to the court should be made in relation to the proceeding."
GIVEN `the court is satisfied there are special reasons other than the parties' convenience` IS A BOOLEAN
      `written notice was given to both Attorneys-General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied a reasonable time has elapsed since the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Supreme Court may order that it determine the proceeding (s 6(3), (4))` `the court is satisfied there are special reasons other than the parties' convenience` `written notice was given to both Attorneys-General` `the court is satisfied a reasonable time has elapsed since the notice` IF
        `the court is satisfied there are special reasons other than the parties' convenience`
    AND `written notice was given to both Attorneys-General`
    AND `the court is satisfied a reasonable time has elapsed since the notice`

-- s 6(5) "For the purposes of subsection (4), the court-- ... (b) may direct a party to the proceeding to give a
-- notice in accordance with that subsection." The Act fixes no time; the court's direction does, so the days allowed
-- are an input. Missing the time is a breach of the direction, and the Supreme Court cannot be satisfied under
-- s 6(4)(a), so cannot make an s 6(3) order, until the notice is given.
DECLARE `Cross-vesting party` IS ONE OF `the directed party`
DECLARE `Cross-vesting action` IS ONE OF `give written notice of the special federal matter to both Attorneys-General`

GIVEN `the days the court allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Cross-vesting party` `Cross-vesting action`
`s 6(5)(b) -- the notice the court directed a party to give` `the days the court allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the directed party`
    MUST `give written notice of the special federal matter to both Attorneys-General`
    WITHIN `the days the court allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the directed party` BECAUSE "the notice the Supreme Court directed under s 6(5)(b) was not given in the time it allowed; until it is given the court cannot make an s 6(3) order (s 6(4)(a))"

-- s 6(7) "Nothing in this section prevents the court granting urgent relief of an interlocutory nature if it is in
-- the interests of justice to do so." When the "if" is not met the section is silent (fork line 2 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the court finds urgent interlocutory relief in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 does not stop urgent interlocutory relief (s 6(7))` `the court finds urgent interlocutory relief in the interests of justice` MEANS
    IF `the court finds urgent interlocutory relief in the interests of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 6(8) "If, through inadvertence, the Supreme Court determines a proceeding of the kind mentioned in subsection (1)
-- without-- (a) the court making an order under subsection (3) ...; or (b) a notice mentioned in subsection (4) being
-- given; nothing in this section invalidates the decision of that court."
-- Answers whether s 6 invalidates the decision: JUST FALSE where s 6(8) says it does not; NOTHING otherwise.
GIVEN `the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without an s 6(3) order or the s 6(4) notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it did so through inadvertence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 invalidates the decision` `the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without an s 6(3) order or the s 6(4) notice` `it did so through inadvertence` MEANS
    IF `the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without an s 6(3) order or the s 6(4) notice` AND `it did so through inadvertence`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 7 -- institution and hearing of appeals`

DECLARE `Decision appealed from` IS ONE OF
    `a single Judge of the Federal Court`
    `a single Judge of the Family Court`
    `the Full Court of the Federal Court`
    `the Full Court of the Family Court`

DECLARE `Appeal court` IS ONE OF
    `the Full Court of the Supreme Court of Queensland`
    `the Federal Court`
    `the Family Court`
    `the High Court`

-- s 7(1) "An appeal shall not be instituted from a decision of a single Judge of the Federal Court or the Family
-- Court to the Full Court of the Supreme Court."
-- s 7(2) "An appeal shall not be instituted from the Federal Court or the Family Court to the other of those courts."
-- "Full Court, in relation to a Supreme Court of a State, includes any court of the State to which appeals lie from a
-- single Judge of that Supreme Court" (s 3(1)): in Queensland, the Court of Appeal.
GIVEN `from` IS A `Decision appealed from`
      `to`   IS AN `Appeal court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an appeal may be instituted from the federal court (s 7(1), (2))` `from` `to` MEANS
    IF `from a single Judge` AND `to the Full Court of the Supreme Court`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF (`from the Federal Court` AND `to the Family Court`) OR (`from the Family Court` AND `to the Federal Court`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `from a single Judge` MEANS
            CONSIDER `from`
            WHEN `a single Judge of the Federal Court` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a single Judge of the Family Court` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `from the Federal Court` MEANS
            CONSIDER `from`
            WHEN `a single Judge of the Federal Court` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the Full Court of the Federal Court` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `from the Family Court` MEANS
            CONSIDER `from`
            WHEN `a single Judge of the Family Court` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the Full Court of the Family Court` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `to the Full Court of the Supreme Court` MEANS
            CONSIDER `to`
            WHEN `the Full Court of the Supreme Court of Queensland` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `to the Family Court` MEANS
            CONSIDER `to`
            WHEN `the Family Court` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `to the Federal Court` MEANS
            CONSIDER `to`
            WHEN `the Federal Court` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Appeal route answer` IS ONE OF
    `only in the Full Court of the Supreme Court (s 7(3))`
    `only in the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires, or, with special leave, the High Court (s 7(4))`
    `it may be dealt with as if no matter arose under a Schedule Act (s 7(5))`

-- s 7(3) "Where it appears that the only matters for determination in a proceeding by way of an appeal from a
-- decision of a single Judge of the Supreme Court are matters other than matters arising under an Act specified in
-- the Schedule to the Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (Cwlth), that proceeding shall be instituted
-- only in, and shall be determined only by, the Full Court of the Supreme Court."
-- s 7(4) "Subject to subsections (6) and (7), where it appears that a matter for determination in a proceeding by way
-- of an appeal from a decision of a single Judge of the Supreme Court (not being a proceeding to which subsection (5)
-- applies) is a matter arising under an Act specified in the Schedule ..., that proceeding shall be instituted only
-- in, and shall be determined only by-- (a) the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case
-- requires; or (b) with special leave of the High Court, the High Court."
-- s 7(5) "A proceeding by way of an appeal from a decision of a Judge of a State Family Court, being a proceeding
-- involving the determination of-- (a) a matter arising under an Act specified in the Schedule ...; and (b) another
-- matter; may be dealt with as if no matter for determination in the proceeding were a matter arising under an Act
-- specified in that Schedule."
GIVEN `a matter arises under an Act in the Commonwealth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision was a State Family Court Judge's and the appeal also involves another matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Appeal route answer`
`the s 7 appeal route` `a matter arises under an Act in the Commonwealth Schedule` `the decision was a State Family Court Judge's and the appeal also involves another matter` MEANS
    IF NOT `a matter arises under an Act in the Commonwealth Schedule`
    THEN `only in the Full Court of the Supreme Court (s 7(3))`
    ELSE IF `the decision was a State Family Court Judge's and the appeal also involves another matter`
         THEN `it may be dealt with as if no matter arose under a Schedule Act (s 7(5))`
         ELSE `only in the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires, or, with special leave, the High Court (s 7(4))`

-- s 7(6) "Where-- (a) the Full Court of the Supreme Court commences to hear a proceeding by way of an appeal; and (b)
-- before the Court determines the proceeding, it appears to the Court that the proceeding is a proceeding to which
-- subsection (4) applies; the Court shall, unless the interests of justice require that the Court proceed to
-- determine the proceeding, transfer the proceeding to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as
-- the case requires."
GIVEN `the Full Court has begun to hear the appeal and not yet determined it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Full Court that s 7(4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interests of justice require the Full Court to go on` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Full Court must transfer the appeal (s 7(6))` `the Full Court has begun to hear the appeal and not yet determined it` `it appears to the Full Court that s 7(4) applies` `the interests of justice require the Full Court to go on` IF
        `the Full Court has begun to hear the appeal and not yet determined it`
    AND `it appears to the Full Court that s 7(4) applies`
    AND (NOT `the interests of justice require the Full Court to go on`)

-- s 7(7) "Where the Full Court of the Supreme Court-- (a) determines a proceeding to which subsection (4) applies as
-- mentioned in subsection (6); or (b) through inadvertence, determines a proceeding to which subsection (4) applies;
-- nothing in this section invalidates the decision of that Court."
GIVEN `the Full Court decided an s 7(4) appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it went on because the interests of justice required it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it did so through inadvertence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7 invalidates the decision` `the Full Court decided an s 7(4) appeal` `it went on because the interests of justice required it` `it did so through inadvertence` MEANS
    IF `the Full Court decided an s 7(4) appeal` AND (`it went on because the interests of justice required it` OR `it did so through inadvertence`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 8 -- orders by the Supreme Court (removal)`

-- s 8(1) "Where-- (a) a proceeding (the relevant proceeding) is pending in-- (i) a court, other than the Supreme Court,
-- of the State; or (ii) a tribunal established by or under an Act; and (b) it appears to the Supreme Court that-- (i)
-- the relevant proceeding arises out of, or is related to, another proceeding pending in the Federal Court, the
-- Family Court or the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory and, if an order is made under this subsection
-- in relation to the relevant proceeding, there would be grounds on which that other proceeding could be transferred
-- to the Supreme Court; or (ii) an order should be made under this subsection in relation to the relevant proceeding
-- so that consideration can be given to whether the relevant proceeding should be transferred to another court; the
-- Supreme Court may, on the application of a party to the relevant proceeding or of its own motion, make an order
-- removing the relevant proceeding to the Supreme Court."
GIVEN `the court it is pending in` IS A `Court`
      `a related proceeding is pending in the Federal Court, the Family Court or another Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Supreme Court finds there would be grounds to transfer that other proceeding to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Supreme Court finds removal should be made so a transfer can be considered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Supreme Court may remove the proceeding (s 8(1))` `the court it is pending in` `a related proceeding is pending in the Federal Court, the Family Court or another Supreme Court` `the Supreme Court finds there would be grounds to transfer that other proceeding to it` `the Supreme Court finds removal should be made so a transfer can be considered` IF
        `it is pending in a lower Queensland court or a tribunal`
    AND (   (    `a related proceeding is pending in the Federal Court, the Family Court or another Supreme Court`
             AND `the Supreme Court finds there would be grounds to transfer that other proceeding to it`)
         OR `the Supreme Court finds removal should be made so a transfer can be considered`)
    WHERE
        `it is pending in a lower Queensland court or a tribunal` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the court it is pending in`
            WHEN `a court of Queensland other than the Supreme Court` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a tribunal established by or under an Act` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 8(3) "Where a proceeding is removed to the Supreme Court in accordance with an order made under subsection (1),
-- the Supreme Court may, if the Supreme Court considers it appropriate to do so, remit the proceeding to the court or
-- tribunal from which the proceeding was removed."
GIVEN `the proceeding was removed under s 8(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Supreme Court considers remitting it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Supreme Court may remit the proceeding (s 8(3))` `the proceeding was removed under s 8(1)` `the Supreme Court considers remitting it appropriate` IF
        `the proceeding was removed under s 8(1)`
    AND `the Supreme Court considers remitting it appropriate`

§§ `s 9, s 10 -- the Supreme Court's jurisdiction; consumer law matters`

-- s 9 "The Supreme Court-- (a) may exercise jurisdiction ... conferred on that court by a provision of this Act or of
-- a law of the Commonwealth or a State relating to cross-vesting of jurisdiction; and (b) may hear and determine a
-- proceeding transferred to that court under such a provision."
GIVEN `the proceeding was transferred to the Supreme Court of Queensland under a cross-vesting provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Supreme Court may hear the transferred proceeding (s 9)` `the proceeding was transferred to the Supreme Court of Queensland under a cross-vesting provision` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding was transferred to the Supreme Court of Queensland under a cross-vesting provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 10 "Where-- (a) a proceeding is pending in the Supreme Court or the Supreme Court of another State or of a
-- Territory; and (b) a matter for determination in the proceeding is a matter arising under any of the following
-- provisions of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 (Cwlth), schedule 2, applying as a law of the Commonwealth--
-- chapter 3, part 3-1, divisions 1, 2, 4 or 5; chapter 3, part 3-3; chapter 3, part 3-4; and (c) no matter for
-- determination in the proceeding is a special federal matter; and (d) the proceeding is not a proceeding by way of
-- an appeal from a judgment of a court; and (e) a court of the State, other than the Supreme Court, has jurisdiction
-- with respect to all of the matters for determination in the proceeding; the court referred to in paragraph (a) may
-- on the application of a party to the proceeding or of its own motion, transfer the proceeding to the court referred
-- to in paragraph (e)."
GIVEN `the court it is pending in` IS A `Court`
      `a matter arises under the listed Australian Consumer Law provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no matter is a special federal matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an appeal from a judgment of a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a lower Queensland court has jurisdiction over all the matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may transfer the consumer law proceeding to a lower Queensland court (s 10)` `the court it is pending in` `a matter arises under the listed Australian Consumer Law provisions` `no matter is a special federal matter` `it is an appeal from a judgment of a court` `a lower Queensland court has jurisdiction over all the matters` IF
        `it is pending in a Supreme Court s 10 names`
    AND `a matter arises under the listed Australian Consumer Law provisions`
    AND `no matter is a special federal matter`
    AND (NOT `it is an appeal from a judgment of a court`)
    AND `a lower Queensland court has jurisdiction over all the matters`
    WHERE
        `it is pending in a Supreme Court s 10 names` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the court it is pending in`
            WHEN `the Supreme Court of Queensland` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 11, s 12 -- conduct of proceedings; costs`

DECLARE `Applicable law answer` IS ONE OF
    `the written and unwritten law of the other State or Territory under whose written law the right of action arises (s 11(1)(b))`
    `the law in force in the State or Territory where the court is sitting, including its choice of law rules (s 11(1)(a))`
    `section 11 does not apply: the court is not exercising cross-vested jurisdiction`

-- s 11(1) "Where it appears to a court that the court will, or will be likely to, in determining a matter for
-- determination in a proceeding, be exercising jurisdiction conferred by this Act or by a law of the Commonwealth or
-- a State relating to cross-vesting of jurisdiction-- (a) subject to paragraphs (b) and (c), the court shall ... apply
-- the law in force in the State or Territory in which the court is sitting (including choice of law rules); and (b)
-- subject to paragraph (c), if that matter is a right of action arising under a written law of another State or
-- Territory, the court shall ... apply the written and unwritten law of that other State or Territory; and (c) the
-- rules of evidence and procedure ... shall be such as the court considers appropriate in the circumstances, being
-- rules that are applied in a superior court in Australia or in an external Territory."
GIVEN `the court is likely to exercise cross-vested jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right of action arises under a written law of another State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Applicable law answer`
`the s 11 applicable law` `the court is likely to exercise cross-vested jurisdiction` `the right of action arises under a written law of another State or Territory` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court is likely to exercise cross-vested jurisdiction`
    THEN `section 11 does not apply: the court is not exercising cross-vested jurisdiction`
    ELSE IF `the right of action arises under a written law of another State or Territory`
         THEN `the written and unwritten law of the other State or Territory under whose written law the right of action arises (s 11(1)(b))`
         ELSE `the law in force in the State or Territory where the court is sitting, including its choice of law rules (s 11(1)(a))`

-- s 11(3) "Where a proceeding is transferred or removed to a court (the transferee court) from another court (the
-- transferor court), the transferee court shall deal with the proceeding as if, subject to any order of the
-- transferee court, the steps that had been taken for the purposes of the proceeding in the transferor court
-- (including the making of an order), or similar steps, had been taken in the transferee court."
-- An order of the transferee court that a step is not to count displaces it (fork line 3 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the proceeding was transferred or removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferee court ordered otherwise for the step` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the earlier step counts in the transferee court (s 11(3))` `the proceeding was transferred or removed` `the transferee court ordered otherwise for the step` IF
        `the proceeding was transferred or removed`
    AND (NOT `the transferee court ordered otherwise for the step`)

-- s 12 "Where a proceeding is transferred or removed to a court, that court may make an order as to costs that relate
-- to the conduct of the proceeding before the transfer or removal if those costs have not already been dealt with by
-- another court."
GIVEN `the proceeding was transferred or removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another court has already dealt with those costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the new court may order the earlier costs (s 12)` `the proceeding was transferred or removed` `another court has already dealt with those costs` IF
        `the proceeding was transferred or removed`
    AND (NOT `another court has already dealt with those costs`)

§§ `s 13, s 14 -- appeals; enforcement`

DECLARE `Decision kind` IS ONE OF
    `a decision about transferring or removing the proceeding under this Act`
    `a decision about which rules of evidence and procedure apply under s 11(1)`
    `some other decision`

-- s 13 "An appeal does not lie from a decision of a court-- (a) in relation to the transfer or removal of a
-- proceeding under this act; or (b) as to which rules of evidence and procedure are to be applied pursuant to section
-- 11(1)."
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Decision kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an appeal lies from the decision (s 13)` `the decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a decision about transferring or removing the proceeding under this Act` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a decision about which rules of evidence and procedure apply under s 11(1)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `some other decision` THEN NOTHING

-- s 14(1) "A judgment of the Supreme Court that is given, in whole or in part, in the exercise of jurisdiction
-- conferred by a law or laws relating to cross-vesting of jurisdiction is enforceable in the State as if the
-- judgment had been given entirely in the exercise of the jurisdiction of the Supreme Court apart from any such law."
GIVEN `it is a Supreme Court of Queensland judgment given at least in part in cross-vested jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the judgment is enforceable as an ordinary Supreme Court judgment (s 14(1))` `it is a Supreme Court of Queensland judgment given at least in part in cross-vested jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `it is a Supreme Court of Queensland judgment given at least in part in cross-vested jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
